{
  "width": 612.0,
  "height": 792.0,
  "lines": [
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "SPQR: Great Battles of the",
      "x0": 207.9424,
      "top": 28.058200000000056,
      "x1": 306.0,
      "bottom": 37.058200000000056
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "heavy infantry, the last of the Roman hoplites. By the end of this",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 54.003600000000006,
      "x1": 296.9769999999999,
      "bottom": 64.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "period, they were starting to disappear as a unit class.",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 66.0036,
      "x1": 258.56999999999994,
      "bottom": 76.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "Alae Sociorum: The “wings of the allies” (which is",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 83.4036000000001,
      "x1": 297.011,
      "bottom": 93.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "what the words mean in Latin) of the consular army.",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 95.4036000000001,
      "x1": 297.01099999999997,
      "bottom": 105.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "Each ala (and there were two for each army) was",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 107.4036000000001,
      "x1": 297.016,
      "bottom": 117.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "raised from non-citizen allies of Rome (e.g., Sam-",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 119.4036000000001,
      "x1": 297.01,
      "bottom": 129.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "nites, Campanians, Umbrians) and organized in somewhat",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 131.4036000000001,
      "x1": 297.0349999999998,
      "bottom": 141.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "similar fashion to the legion. However, each ala had fewer Velites",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 143.4036000000001,
      "x1": 296.9439999999996,
      "bottom": 153.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "and Triarii, the differences between the Hastati and Principes",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 155.4036000000001,
      "x1": 297.01899999999995,
      "bottom": 165.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "tended to disappear, and, because they were usually better at that",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 167.4036000000001,
      "x1": 297.02899999999966,
      "bottom": 177.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "sort of thing, they had three times the cavalry contingent as did",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 179.4036000000001,
      "x1": 297.0239999999999,
      "bottom": 189.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "the legion. Each ala also had elite cohorts of infantry, the ex-",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 191.4036000000001,
      "x1": 297.0139999999999,
      "bottom": 201.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "traordinarii, and there was a similar cavalry unit for every two",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 203.4036000000001,
      "x1": 297.0079999999998,
      "bottom": 213.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "alae. In all, the organization of each ala more strongly resembled",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 215.4036000000001,
      "x1": 297.0829999999998,
      "bottom": 225.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "the legion of the Empire than that of the Republic. By the time",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 227.4036000000001,
      "x1": 297.03299999999996,
      "bottom": 237.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "of Marius, the alae disappeared to become regular legions, and",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 239.4036000000001,
      "x1": 297.0119999999999,
      "bottom": 249.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "the word ala then referred to cavalry.",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 251.4036000000001,
      "x1": 192.32900000000006,
      "bottom": 261.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "Maniple: Each line of Hastati and Principes fought in maniples,",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 268.8036000000001,
      "x1": 297.018,
      "bottom": 278.8036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "ten per legion line. They often arrayed in checkerboard, quincunx",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 280.8036,
      "x1": 297.1029999999998,
      "bottom": 290.8036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "fashion which, together with their training, allowed them to move",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 292.8036,
      "x1": 297.09800000000047,
      "bottom": 302.8036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "back and forth through each other, giving the manipular legion",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 304.8036,
      "x1": 297.01199999999994,
      "bottom": 314.8036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "a remarkable flexibility on the battlefield.",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 316.8036,
      "x1": 210.54000000000005,
      "bottom": 326.8036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "Heavy Infantry: Descendants of the Greek hoplites,",
      "x0": 90.4782,
      "top": 334.2036,
      "x1": 297.0882,
      "bottom": 344.2036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "these are troops protected by armor (usually helmet,",
      "x0": 90.4982,
      "top": 346.2036,
      "x1": 297.0132,
      "bottom": 356.2036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "breastplate, and leg armor), carrying a shield, and",
      "x0": 90.4982,
      "top": 358.2036,
      "x1": 297.0122,
      "bottom": 368.2036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "brandishing a sword and perhaps a spear. These were",
      "x0": 90.4982,
      "top": 370.2036,
      "x1": 297.0362,
      "bottom": 380.2036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "powerful units that often fought in densely packed formations",
      "x0": 44.9982,
      "top": 382.2036,
      "x1": 297.00219999999985,
      "bottom": 392.2036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "that restricted their mobility.",
      "x0": 44.9982,
      "top": 394.2036,
      "x1": 158.7632,
      "bottom": 404.2036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "Phalanx: A formation of shoulder-to-",
      "x0": 126.9056,
      "top": 411.6036,
      "x1": 296.6466000000001,
      "bottom": 421.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "shoulder hoplites used in Greek warfare",
      "x0": 126.49560000000001,
      "top": 423.6036,
      "x1": 296.98560000000003,
      "bottom": 433.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "since around the 7th century BCE and",
      "x0": 126.49560000000001,
      "top": 435.6036,
      "x1": 297.0456000000001,
      "bottom": 445.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "perfected by the Macedonians. By the era",
      "x0": 126.49560000000001,
      "top": 447.6036,
      "x1": 297.01060000000007,
      "bottom": 457.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "of Roman ascendancy, the Phalanx had reached the zenith of its",
      "x0": 44.99560000000001,
      "top": 459.6036,
      "x1": 297.0085999999999,
      "bottom": 469.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "development. The front ranks now used a shortened, 9-foot spear,",
      "x0": 44.99560000000001,
      "top": 471.6036,
      "x1": 297.0575999999997,
      "bottom": 481.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "while the fifth rank used an immense 21-footer, with the length",
      "x0": 44.99560000000001,
      "top": 483.6036,
      "x1": 297.01259999999996,
      "bottom": 493.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "of the sarissa of intervening ranks of corresponding lengths. This",
      "x0": 44.99560000000001,
      "top": 495.6036,
      "x1": 297.1315999999999,
      "bottom": 505.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "allowed the Phalanx to present an almost impenetrable wall of",
      "x0": 44.99560000000001,
      "top": 507.6036,
      "x1": 296.9955999999999,
      "bottom": 517.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "spears. Tangentially, as a Roman legionary needed room to swing",
      "x0": 44.99560000000001,
      "top": 519.6035999999999,
      "x1": 297.0285999999998,
      "bottom": 529.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "his sword while the phalangite simply had to remain in place,",
      "x0": 44.99560000000001,
      "top": 531.6035999999999,
      "x1": 296.9986,
      "bottom": 541.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "the ratio of spears to legionary was often (and usually) 10-1!!",
      "x0": 44.99560000000001,
      "top": 543.6035999999999,
      "x1": 296.99559999999997,
      "bottom": 553.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "The trick (and the catch) was the Phalanx remaining in place!",
      "x0": 44.99560000000001,
      "top": 555.6035999999999,
      "x1": 297.0135999999999,
      "bottom": 565.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "The make-up of a Phalanx often varied from country to country,",
      "x0": 44.99560000000001,
      "top": 567.6035999999999,
      "x1": 297.0175999999999,
      "bottom": 577.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "depending on weapon type and training. The ultimate decider,",
      "x0": 44.99560000000001,
      "top": 579.6035999999999,
      "x1": 297.00259999999986,
      "bottom": 589.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "in game terms, was how they were trained tactically.",
      "x0": 44.99560000000001,
      "top": 591.6035999999999,
      "x1": 254.82459999999998,
      "bottom": 601.6035999999999
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "Legion Infantry: A game term used to separate the",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 609.0036,
      "x1": 296.992,
      "bottom": 619.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "Hastati, Principes, and cohorts from the somewhat",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 621.0036,
      "x1": 296.99999999999994,
      "bottom": 631.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "outdated heavy infantry, to whom they were supe-",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 633.0036,
      "x1": 297.0009999999999,
      "bottom": 643.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "rior in mobility and killing power, although often",
      "x0": 90.5,
      "top": 645.0036,
      "x1": 297.049,
      "bottom": 655.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "similarly armed and protected. The major difference is the reli-",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 657.0036,
      "x1": 297.0,
      "bottom": 667.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "ance on the sword, rather than the spear, as a killing weapon, and",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 669.0036,
      "x1": 297.11199999999985,
      "bottom": 679.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "the incorporation of the larger, more effective Roman shield as",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 681.0036,
      "x1": 297.002,
      "bottom": 691.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "fair protection against the spear-armed heavy infantry.",
      "x0": 45.0,
      "top": 693.0036,
      "x1": 261.558,
      "bottom": 703.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "left",
      "text": "© 2026 GMT",
      "x0": 262.6113,
      "top": 750.7607,
      "x1": 305.5793,
      "bottom": 758.7607
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "5",
      "x0": 562.2,
      "top": 25.053600000000074,
      "x1": 567.2,
      "bottom": 35.053600000000074
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "e Roman Republic – 5th Ed.",
      "x0": 306.0,
      "top": 28.058200000000056,
      "x1": 404.0602,
      "bottom": 37.058200000000056
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "Medium Infantry: An ersatz term that applies to",
      "x0": 360.5062,
      "top": 54.4036000000001,
      "x1": 567.0752000000001,
      "bottom": 64.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "units (e.g., Celtic infantry) that, while not as well-",
      "x0": 360.4962,
      "top": 66.4036000000001,
      "x1": 567.0142000000001,
      "bottom": 76.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "equipped as their heavier counterparts, had weap-",
      "x0": 360.4962,
      "top": 78.4036000000001,
      "x1": 567.0162000000001,
      "bottom": 88.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "onry and some body protection that was superior in",
      "x0": 360.4962,
      "top": 90.4036000000001,
      "x1": 566.9812,
      "bottom": 100.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "effectiveness to that worn (or not worn) by light infantry.",
      "x0": 314.9962,
      "top": 102.4036000000001,
      "x1": 542.9941999999999,
      "bottom": 112.4036000000001
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "Barbarian Infantry: Remarkably aggressive, but",
      "x0": 360.5272,
      "top": 119.80360000000007,
      "x1": 567.0822000000001,
      "bottom": 129.80360000000007
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "sometimes tactically dense tribesmen, fighting with",
      "x0": 360.4972,
      "top": 131.80360000000007,
      "x1": 566.9992,
      "bottom": 141.80360000000007
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "huge swords, vicious battle axes, minimal body ar-",
      "x0": 360.4972,
      "top": 143.80360000000007,
      "x1": 566.9972000000001,
      "bottom": 153.80360000000007
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "mor, but lots of courage—the latter typically good",
      "x0": 360.4972000000001,
      "top": 155.80360000000007,
      "x1": 566.9892000000001,
      "bottom": 165.80360000000007
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "for one charge only. They could, when led and used correctly,",
      "x0": 314.9972000000001,
      "top": 167.80360000000007,
      "x1": 567.0142,
      "bottom": 177.80360000000007
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "be extremely effective (and frightening, so much so that the",
      "x0": 314.9972000000001,
      "top": 179.80360000000007,
      "x1": 567.1312000000003,
      "bottom": 189.80360000000007
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "Romans took to emulating their ‘battle cry’). Far too often they",
      "x0": 314.9972000000001,
      "top": 191.80360000000007,
      "x1": 567.0062,
      "bottom": 201.80360000000007
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "were just an unruly mob that disintegrated when faced with",
      "x0": 314.9972000000001,
      "top": 203.80360000000007,
      "x1": 567.1272000000001,
      "bottom": 213.80360000000007
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "superior organization.",
      "x0": 314.9972000000001,
      "top": 215.80360000000007,
      "x1": 402.5752000000001,
      "bottom": 225.80360000000007
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "Light Infantry: A generic term applied to foot units",
      "x0": 360.5,
      "top": 233.20360000000005,
      "x1": 566.998,
      "bottom": 243.20360000000005
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "with little or no body armor, a light shield, and usu-",
      "x0": 360.5,
      "top": 245.20360000000005,
      "x1": 567.0130000000001,
      "bottom": 255.20360000000005
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "ally a spear and/or sword. Most light infantry had",
      "x0": 360.5,
      "top": 257.20360000000005,
      "x1": 567.01,
      "bottom": 267.20360000000005
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "missile capability, although their tactics and training",
      "x0": 360.5,
      "top": 269.20360000000005,
      "x1": 567.0129999999999,
      "bottom": 279.20360000000005
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "made them different from skirmishers.",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 281.2036,
      "x1": 468.94800000000004,
      "bottom": 291.2036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "Skirmishers: A generic term applied to troops that wore no ar-",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 298.6036,
      "x1": 567.0000000000001,
      "bottom": 308.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "mor, rarely carried shields, and used missiles: javelinists, archers",
      "x0": 315.00000000000006,
      "top": 310.6036,
      "x1": 567.0799999999999,
      "bottom": 320.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "and slingers. Their role was to harass and annoy the approaching",
      "x0": 315.00000000000006,
      "top": 322.6036,
      "x1": 567.0029999999998,
      "bottom": 332.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "enemy and present a screen behind which, hopefully, movement",
      "x0": 315.00000000000006,
      "top": 334.6036,
      "x1": 567.025,
      "bottom": 344.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "could be concealed. Their mobility allowed them to outrun their",
      "x0": 315.00000000000006,
      "top": 346.6036,
      "x1": 567.014,
      "bottom": 356.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "weightier opponents, which, all things considered, was their best",
      "x0": 315.00000000000006,
      "top": 358.6036,
      "x1": 567.0900000000001,
      "bottom": 368.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "bet for survival. They rarely, if ever, shock-attacked, as they had",
      "x0": 315.00000000000006,
      "top": 370.6036,
      "x1": 567.0089999999999,
      "bottom": 380.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "no weapons with which to do so, and they deployed in dispersed,",
      "x0": 315.00000000000006,
      "top": 382.6036,
      "x1": 567.0800000000002,
      "bottom": 392.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "amorphous formations which gave them great flexibility in terms",
      "x0": 315.00000000000006,
      "top": 394.6036,
      "x1": 566.944,
      "bottom": 404.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "of maneuvering.",
      "x0": 315.00000000000006,
      "top": 406.6036,
      "x1": 380.5400000000001,
      "bottom": 416.6036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "Javelinists: Skirmishers that used a thrown spear as",
      "x0": 360.5,
      "top": 424.0036,
      "x1": 566.99,
      "bottom": 434.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "their weapon of harassment. Essentially, the era sees",
      "x0": 360.5,
      "top": 436.0036,
      "x1": 566.992,
      "bottom": 446.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "few pure javelinist skirmishers, as the weapon was",
      "x0": 360.5,
      "top": 448.0036,
      "x1": 567.009,
      "bottom": 458.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "proving to be inefficient when used alone, which is",
      "x0": 360.5,
      "top": 460.0036,
      "x1": 567.0,
      "bottom": 470.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "why there are no javelinist skirmishers in the game. By this time,",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 472.0036,
      "x1": 567.0300000000002,
      "bottom": 482.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "most foot soldiers carried a javelin or two which they threw",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 484.0036,
      "x1": 566.9400000000003,
      "bottom": 494.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "prior to closing for combat.",
      "x0": 315.0,
      "top": 496.0036,
      "x1": 424.71000000000004,
      "bottom": 506.0036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "Archers: Light troops (virtually no armor/protection),",
      "x0": 360.3673,
      "top": 513.4036,
      "x1": 567.2222999999998,
      "bottom": 523.4036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "usually from Crete, that fired about 30+ arrows an",
      "x0": 360.4973,
      "top": 525.4036,
      "x1": 566.9993000000001,
      "bottom": 535.4036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "effective distance of 150+ yards, with a maximum",
      "x0": 360.4973,
      "top": 537.4036,
      "x1": 567.0052999999999,
      "bottom": 547.4036
    },
    {
      "column": "right",
      "text": "range of 250 yards (less when mounted and moving).",
      "x0": 360.4973,
      "top": 549.4036,
